Stop the browser app from implying MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT and MOZ_NORMANDY.

Both are project_flags that ONLY accept implied values (possible_origins=
("implied",)), so no mozconfig or environment setting can turn them off —
deleting the imply_option lines is the only way, and it is equivalent to how
Thunderbird ships without them.

Effects of MOZ_NORMANDY being unset (all call sites are guarded upstream):
 - BrowserComponents.manifest: the "browser-before-ui-startup ...
   Normandy.init" category registration is preprocessed out, so the Normandy
   recipe runner can never start;
 - AppConstants.MOZ_NORMANDY becomes false (FirstStartup, Troubleshoot);
 - the Studies section of about:preferences#privacy is compiled out.

MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT has exactly one consumer besides this line: the
MOZ_DATA_REPORTING derivation (telemetry|healthreport|crashreporter|normandy).
With telemetry reporting off (mozconfig), the crash reporter disabled
(--disable-crashreporter), and these two implies gone, MOZ_DATA_REPORTING is
false and the FHR/data-choices upload glue is excluded from the build.

diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -7,7 +7,5 @@
 imply_option("MOZ_PLACES", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_SYNC", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEDICATED_PROFILES", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_BLOCK_PROFILE_DOWNGRADE", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
